#!/bin/bash
# scratch: hypothesis / prediction / rule texts of the runs of the twin / R-arm chain (D67, 2026-11-09), sourced by step_trainsuite.sh. They repeat the card section
# "Seed twin and R arm" (experiments/t22_student_encoder), which was written before any of these runs. No single or double quotes inside the texts.

HYP_R='t22 R arm (card experiments/t22_student_encoder, section Seed twin and R arm; Mirko D67, 2026-11-09): the ResNet-18 student (distilled in t22.A2R_s0 with the A2 recipe, 6 epochs on the large split) replaces the frozen DualBEV + BEVFusion encoders and the res4 depth of the CURRENT frame in the t21 P4 pair chain; everything else as t22.B_s0 (warm start t20.base_s0, 1500 steps, lr 1e-4, student 1e-5, distillation anchor on the current frame). ResNet-18 is 2.6 x faster than the EfficientViT-B1 student at batch 1 (3.4 against 8.8 ms), so if it holds the guards it is the cheaper stand-in'
PRED_R='VAL 1000 frames, dt 0, against t21.pair4_s0 (margins m = max(0.010, half-width) as in t22.B_s0): lane divider IoU@1 -0.005 (range -0.020 .. +0.005), mAP of the fusion area -0.015 (-0.035 .. -0.005), static-cell velocity EPE +0.08 (+0.03 .. +0.13: only the current frame comes from the student), moving-centre EPE +0.05 (+0.02 .. +0.08), vehicle AP@2 at 40 - 60 m within -0.03; image side about 0.19 of the teachers time in fp32; training step 3.9 - 6.5 s. My estimate: STAND-IN about 15 pct, INCONCLUSIVE about 55 pct, CUT about 30 pct'
RULE_R='by hand: composed from the card (section 1 decision rule, unchanged, R in the place of S), one seed: STAND-IN candidate when every guard is not below the control by more than m (point estimate and the lower end of the interval not beyond 2 m) and the cost row holds -> its own seed twin before any adoption (one seed never gives KEEP); BETTER when a map or line guard exceeds +m with the interval excluding 0; CUT when a guard is below the control by more than 2 m with the interval entirely below -m; INCONCLUSIVE when an interval straddles a margin -> this chain ends and Mirko decides (a new mechanism, not another seed)'

HYP_S1='t22 seed twin of stage B, the student (card experiments/t22_student_encoder, section Seed twin and R arm; Mirko D67, 2026-11-09): t22.B_s0 repeated with seed 1 (the same A2 EfficientViT-B1 student checkpoint, same recipe, current-tree code), the matched partner of t21.pair4_s1. Stage B is INCONCLUSIVE on one seed (mAP of the fusion area -0.0127 against a margin 0.0117, static-cell velocity EPE +0.083, moving-centre +0.052) and B2 is CUT; the rule asks for a second seed of the student and of the control'
PRED_S1='VAL 1000 frames, dt 0: the student-minus-control differences of seed 1 (against t21.pair4_s1) repeat those of seed 0 within the seed spread of the control (about 0.005 - 0.010 on the map rows): mAP of the fusion area -0.013 +- 0.012, static-cell EPE +0.08 +- 0.05, moving-centre EPE +0.05 +- 0.03, lane divider IoU@1 -0.005 +- 0.010. My estimate for the pooled twin: STAND-IN about 10 pct, INCONCLUSIVE about 70 pct, CUT about 20 pct'
RULE_S1='by hand: the twin rule of the card section Seed twin and R arm (written before the runs): per guard row and seed d = student - control with its bootstrap half-width h, m = max(0.010, h); pooled d = mean of the two seeds, m = mean of the two m, h = sqrt(h0^2 + h1^2) / 2. STAND-IN confirmed when for every guard d >= -m and d - h >= -2 m, no seed alone meets CUT on any guard and the cost row holds; BETTER when also a map or line guard has d > +m with d - h > 0; CUT when on the same guard both seeds meet CUT or the pooled interval lies entirely below -m with d < -2 m; INCONCLUSIVE otherwise and then the route stops (a different mechanism, not a third seed)'

HYP_C1='t21 P4 pair control, second seed (card experiments/t22_student_encoder, section Seed twin and R arm; Mirko D67, 2026-11-09): t21.pair4_s0 repeated with seed 1 on the current tree, the matched partner of t22.B_s1 and the measure of the control seed spread'
PRED_C1='VAL 1000 frames, dt 0: within 0.010 of t21.pair4_s0 on the map rows (lane divider IoU@1 0.5495, mAP of the fusion area 0.4154), static-cell EPE 0.2172 +- 0.03, moving-centre EPE 1.0911 +- 0.04; no verdict of its own'
RULE_C1='no verdict of its own: partner of t22.B_s1 in the twin rule of the card section Seed twin and R arm; its seed spread against t21.pair4_s0 is reported next to the differences'
